  "reviewer": "visual-agent (repair round, run 21)",
  "notes": "Repair round. The first reviewed mask cut both chair wings in the head band but stopped at the shoulder-arrival row, leaving three strips of the same gaming chair inside the person: x644-694 y514-535 and x603-639 y531-544 on the frame-left shoulder, x992-1073 y504-558 on the frame-right shoulder. Each was measured, not guessed: temporal standard deviation of the plate luma over the whole 43 s is 1.1, 2.4 and 0.8 px-value respectively, while his shoulder two centimetres away wanders by 10; mean luma 12, 32 and 3 against the t-shirt's own 20-32. The shipped matte held its top edge frozen to 0.76 px across columns 596-631 for 216 sampled frames while the flanking shoulder columns moved by 16.4 - furniture, by the pipeline's own frozen-column rule - and that is the black knob on the frame-left shoulder the viewer test rejected. The three exclude polygons follow each measured component's own contour. Nothing of him is touched: cap, both ears, temple, cheek, jaw, beard, chin, neck, both shoulders and the hands keep every pixel they had, and the dark static patch at x705-723 y480-510 beside his jaw was deliberately LEFT IN rather than risk his neck. Ears and jaw re-inspected on the actual first frame at 5x after the edit.",
